{{Quote|Tough hides. Naturally resistant to blaster fire. The Hutts like to use them as bodyguards and bounty hunters.|[[Luke Skywalker]], on Weequay|<ref name="Heir to the Jedi">''[[Heir to the Jedi]]''</ref>}}
'''Weequays''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] from the planet [[Sriluur]] common throughout the galaxy. Weequay possessed tough, [[leather]]y skin resistant to [[desert]] environments and [[blaster]] fire. Many Weequay were [[Mercenary|mercenaries]], [[pirate]]s, and [[bodyguard]]s for the [[Hutt Clan]]. Notable Weequays included [[Hondo Ohnaka]], who led the [[Ohnaka Gang]], and the [[Jedi]] [[Sora Bulq]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:KieraSwan-BHUSC.png|thumb|left|200px|Kiera Swan, a female Weequay bounty hunter]]
Weequay were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[desert]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Sriluur]].<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" /> Weequays were common throughout the galaxy.<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> Evolving under merciless conditions, their tough, [[leather]]y skin helped them endure the harsh environment of their homeworld<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" /> as well as providing natural resistance to [[blaster]] fire. This made Weequays ideal [[bodyguard]]s and [[bounty hunter]]s.<ref name="Heir to the Jedi" /> Some Weequay grew horns on their lower jaw,<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> while others had bumpy extensions of their skin.<ref name="Return of the Jedi" /> Weequays often kept their hair long.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> Weequays possessed the ability to communicate with other nearby Weequays through [[pheromone]]s that were undetectable to non-Weequays.<ref name="GoD">''[[Ghosts of Dathomir]]''</ref> Weequays could also be [[Force-sensitive]].<ref name="Attack of the Clones">{{Film|II}}</ref>

==History==
Many Weequays were involved in a series of [[Houk–Weequay wars|wars]] against the [[Houk]] species.<ref name="Gadgets and Gear">''[[Gadgets and Gear]]''</ref> Many Weequays served the [[Hutt Clan]] as [[Mercenary|mercenaries]], bodyguards, and [[Slavery|slaves]] since the Hutts controlled their homeworld.<ref name="YouTube">{{StarWarsShow|Vwv30DSO52k|Dave Filoni Talks Star Wars: The Clone Wars and Episode IX Begins Shooting!|sw_url=video/dave-filoni-talks-star-wars-the-clone-wars-and-episode-ix-begins-shooting}}</ref> Some were able to escape those hardships and sought out the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and used their skill to bring some good to [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref>

[[File:Weequays.png|thumb|200px|right|Hondo Ohnaka and one of his pirate crew]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], [[Hondo Ohnaka]] and his [[Ohnaka Gang]] became involved in several conflicts with both the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> The [[pirate]] gang operated out of [[Florrum]] but were extirpated by Separatist forces led by [[General]] [[Grievous]].<ref name="Bond">{{TCW|A Necessary Bond}}</ref> Ohnaka and his remaining pirates would work out of the ruins of the base afterward. When a portion of Ohnaka's pirates swore themselves to the ex-[[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]] sometime later, Ohnaka and his loyalist faction defended their ruined base until the gang reunified.<ref name="Revival">{{TCW|Revival (episode)}}</ref> During the [[Imperial Era]], the gang would be dissolved<ref name="Broken Horn">{{Rebels|Brothers of the Broken Horn}}</ref> but later resurface under the leadership of [[Captain]] [[Skragg]].<ref name="Bounty Hunters 8">[[Bounty Hunters 8|''Bounty Hunters'' 8]]</ref>

During the [[New Republic Era]], a Weequay pirate named [[Drell]] was part of the [[Warbird gang]]. Drell and the rest of the gang worked for the [[First Order]] until they were betrayed,<ref name="TDD">{{Resistance|The Doza Dilemma}}</ref> to which the gang responded to by later working with the [[Resistance]].<ref name="AQSR">{{Resistance|A Quick Salvage Run}}</ref>

==Weequay in the galaxy==
[[File:WeequayBartenderMando.png|thumb|left|175px|[[Taanti]], the bartender of the [[Mos Pelgo saloon]].]]
During the [[High Republic Era]], one of the [[Tempest Runner]]s of the [[Nihil]] was the Weequay [[Gender|male]] [[Kassav Milliko]] who served the Nihil until his [[death]] at the [[Battle of Kur]].<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref>

The pirate Hondo Ohnaka was the leader of the Ohnaka Gang. Ohnaka and most of the members, including [[Turk Falso]]<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> [[Gwarm]],<ref name="Bounty Hunters" /> and [[Jiro]]<ref name="Revival">{{TCW|Revival (episode)}}</ref> were Weequay.<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> A Weequay pirate named [[Skragg]] took control of the remnants of the Ohnaka Gang during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Bounty Hunters 8">[[Bounty Hunters 8|''Bounty Hunters'' 8]]</ref> Ohnaka would later assist a rebel group known as the [[Spectres]] with [[Liberation of Lothal|liberating]] the planet [[Lothal]] from the grip of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Family Reunion – & Farewell">{{Rebels|Family Reunion &ndash; and Farewell}}</ref> Ohnaka would later open [[Ohnaka Transport Solutions]] on [[Batuu]].<ref name="Galaxy's Edge">[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge|''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge]]</ref>

Many Weequay worked for the Hutt Cartel, some of which included [[Pagetti Rook]] and [[Rintel Aren]], who specifically worked for [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba the Hutt]]. Both Aren and Rook would meet their demise during the [[Rescue of Han Solo]] at the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]].<ref name="Return of the Jedi" />

Multiple force-sensitive Weequay joined the [[Jedi Order]], including the [[Jedi]] [[Sora Bulq]] and [[Jedi Knight]] [[Que-Mars Redath-Gom]].<ref name="Attack of the Clones" />

==Behind the scenes==
Weequays were created for [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="Return of the Jedi" /> The Weequay species were named after the fictional [[Wikipedia:Polynesia|Polynesian]] harpononer [[Wikipedia:Queequeg|Queequeg]] from [[Wikipedia:Herman Melville|Herman Melville's]] book [[Wikipedia:Moby-Dick|''Moby-Dick'']],<ref name="Databank">{{DB|species|weequay|Weequay}}</ref> but were originally named "Queequay" by the crew of ''Return of the Jedi''.<ref name="I67">{{InsiderCite|67|Set Piece|Set Piece: Jabba's Sail Barge}}</ref>

